There are two problems that I know of with Xasteriods.  I have reported both
to the author.   I have since deleted the program (so I won't waste valuable 
time playing games, shame on you all), so I won't be able to give context diffs.

Bug #1) In function init_asts (or something like that) there is a for loop with
3 statements in it that needs surrounding braces.

Bug #2) In order for Xasteroids to work correctly on arbitrary depth displays,
you need to change the depth parameter in the XCreatePixmap calls from "1"
to "DefaultDepth(disp, 0)".  This will clear up the BadMatch error, since the
program is trying to draw a 1-bit pixmap into an N-bit window.

